        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "From an external point \\(A\\), \\(AK\\) and \\(AL\\) are tangents to a circle at \\(K\\) and \\(L\\), respectively. If \\(AK=(3x+2)\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\) and \\(AL=(5x-6)\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\), find \\(x\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Tangents drawn from the same external point are equal. Hence, \\(AK=AL\\), so \\(3x+2=5x-6\\). Therefore, \\(2x=8\\) and \\(x=4\\).",
