        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "In a triangle, the side lengths are \\(9\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\), \\(10\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\), and \\(17\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\). Find the altitude drawn to the side of length \\(17\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The semiperimeter is \\(s=18\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\). By Heron’s formula, the area is \\(\\sqrt{18(9)(8)(1)}=36\\,\\mathrm{cm^2}\\). If \\(h\\) is the altitude to the \\(17\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\) side, then \\(36=\\frac{1}{2}(17)h\\), so \\(h=\\frac{72}{17}\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
